repository-code: "https://github.com/cesar-andress/spanish_political_discourse_benchmark"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20745403"
abstract: >
  SPDB is a reproducible annotation resource for pragmatic-function coding in
  Spanish parliamentary discourse. Version 1.0.1 is a provenance and metadata
  patch over v1.0.0: primary Wave-1 dual-coder labels and agreement metrics are
  unchanged (N=100; observed agreement 0.350; Cohen kappa ~0.235;
  Krippendorff alpha ~0.223; Fleiss kappa ~0.219; 65 disagreements). Exploratory
  post-hoc disagreement-cause labels are documented as AI-assisted and not
  independently human-verified. Revised codebook-v1.1.0 remains unvalidated.
  This release is not an adjudicated gold benchmark.
keywords:
  - Spanish political discourse
  - parliamentary discourse
  - pragmatics
  - pragmatic function
  - corpus annotation
  - inter-annotator agreement
  - annotation disagreement
  - language resources
